{"t": 717.602, "n": 296, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I fixed the two lines the review flagged and tidied a few nearby ones. Nothing was run: there's no shell here, so the suite and the structure check haven't been run. The sizes below were measured with a multi-line text search.\n\n## The two flagged findings\n- **BUD-B17** (`budgets-and-failures.spec.md`): I dropped the reason clause \"the usage limit being its only cause\". I also renamed the heading to \"A usage limit spends no counter\", so it states the rule and doesn't echo the task's wording.\n- **DUR-B12** (`durability-and-resume.spec.md`): the scenario that copied the task's \"retry budget of 2\" now uses a budget of 3. The \"reset instant is an hour ahead\" scenario now reads \"whose reset instant has not passed\".\n\n## Other lines I changed\nThese are all in behaviours and criteria that this task added. No existing spec line changed.\n- **BUD-AC15, HUM-AC10:** I removed the task's fixture numbers (retry budget of 2, reset one hour ahead, first run and two resumes). BUD-AC15 now says the refused sessions outnumber the retry budget.\n- **HUM-B14:** the resume command with no `--decision` is now part of the behaviour sentence, not a scenario that referred to \"that pause\". I name it in prose because HUM-B2 calls the field `resume_command` while the code writes `resume`. That mismatch is older than the task and is left alone.\n- **DUR-B13:** the row key is now stated as the latest reset among the thread's pending pauses for a usage limit. It has a \"two pending gates\" scenario and a matching DUR-AC11. The old wording (\"the sessions its pauses wait on\") was loose.\n- **DUR-B12 / BUD-B17 wording:** \"before it\" became \"before that session ran\", and \"the node ends\" became \"the attempt ends\".\n\n## Checks\n- **Ids:** all 8 new behaviours and 8 new criteria are defined once across `plugins/`, and each behaviour is named by its criterion.\n- **Sizes (lines / bytes):**\n\n| Spec | Lines | Bytes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `budgets-and-failures` | 151 | 21,413 |\n| `durability-and-resume` | 110 | 11,451 |\n| `gate-and-human` | 118 | 11,183 |\n| `judge-and-verdict` | 109 | 12,539 |\n| `run-detail-document` | 143 | 15,556 |\n| `run-events` | 192 | 23,746 |\n\n  All are within 400 lines and 30,720 bytes. The previous hand-off only bounded these.\n- **Neighbouring rules:** CLI-B10, RRN-B19, CNL-B15 and CTS-B9 don't contradict the new rules. `engine-cli.spec.md` needs no edit.\n- **Hand-off claims:** I confirmed its code claims and line ranges against the source. I also added test helpers, the two-gate fixture and three neighbouring specs to its reading list.\n\n## Hand-off notes\n- The triage lists no owner decisions. The conversation value and the owner's answers were placeholders, so I treated the run as unattended.\n- The two open questions stay, each with its default: whether a plain resume writes an intervention row, and whether `proceed` is accepted at this pause.\n\nARTIFACT handoff: docs/tasks/i153.handoff.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "a447bda0-d58f-4ba5-8711-46237d7c4aa1"}
